      ":question/problem": "Express $-\\frac{8}{5}\\sin^2\\left(122^\\circ\\right)+\\frac{4}{5}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&-\\frac{8}{5}\\sin^2\\left(122^\\circ\\right)+\\frac{4}{5}\\\\&=\\frac{4}{5}\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(122^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n1-2\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=122^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-2\\sin^2\\left(122^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 122^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(244^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{5}\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(122^\\circ\\right)\\right)&=\\frac{4}{5}\\cos\\left(244^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
